  "question": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\qt0208_23f922a67800.png\"><br>\nIn hydrogen azide, the bond orders of bonds (I) and (II) are ______."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\nI $ < 2$, II $>2$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\nI $>2$, II $>2$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\nI$>2$, II $ < 2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\nI $ < 2$, II $ < 2$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "As in the resonance structure of hydrogen azide, it can be seen that number of $\\mathrm{N}-\\mathrm{N}$ bonds is $\\leq 2$\n<img src=\"assets\\st0208_3a6ff140f0a6.png\"><br>\nHence for bond (I), bond order will be $ < 2$ whereas for bond (II), number of bond $\\geq 2$. \nThus its bond order will be $>2$."
  }
}